agent.py,src/llms/agent.py,ea194e169758b8e4fcf78928598fc937fcf9a2a7,SacSresta/gitpod_autoce,https://api.github.com/repositories/1026564049/contents/src/llms/agent.py?ref=adb808f39954f6fb44d0a255416a2ba5d249123d,https://api.github.com/repositories/1026564049/git/blobs/ea194e169758b8e4fcf78928598fc937fcf9a2a7,https://github.com/SacSresta/gitpod_autoce/blob/adb808f39954f6fb44d0a255416a2ba5d249123d/src/llms/agent.py,,,0,0,0,2,2025-07-26T06:59:23Z,0,0,"# Cold Email Generator

This project generates personalized cold emails using LLMs, LangChain, and several integrated APIs. It supports features like search, database storage, and authentication using cloud services.

## Setup Instructions

### 1. Clone the Repository

Clone the project to your local machine:

git clone https://github.com/SacSresta/gitpod_autoce.git  
cd gitpod_autoce

### 2. Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file in the project root with the following contents. These keys are essential for the app to function correctly:

GROQ_API_KEY=<your_groq_api_key>  
LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2=true  
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY=lsv2_<your_langchain_api_key>  
LANGCHAIN_PROJECT=Cold Email Generator  
LANGCHAIN_ENDPOINT=https://api.s  
TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-dev-<your_tavily_key>  
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://<your-db-user>@<your-db-host>/<your-db-name>  
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=536994689611-<your-client-id>.apps.googleusercontent.com  
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-<your-google-secret>

Make sure this `.env` file is listed in your `.gitignore` to prevent it from being committed.

### 3. Google Cloud Credentials

Download your `credentials.json` file from the Google Cloud Console. This file is used for OAuth or access to services like Google NLP. Place it in the root of the project directory:

/project-root/credentials.json

This file should also be listed in your `.gitignore`.

### 4. Install Dependencies

Install the required Python packages using:

pip install -r requirements.txt

### 5. (Optional) Run with Docker

If you prefer using Docker, build and run the container like so:

docker build -t cold-email-generator .  
docker run --env-file .env cold-email-generator

## Security Tips

- Never commit `.env` or `credentials.json` to your repository.  
- Use `.gitignore` to keep secrets and config files private.  
- Regenerate any keys immediately if they are accidentally pushed.

## Contact

For support, contact [SacSresta](https://github.com/SacSresta) or open an issue on the repository.
