main.py,app/main.py,1815a96355f9de8e5a80ee7eba0b8fa119acc0fe,ujsolon/streamlit_chat,https://api.github.com/repositories/999937896/contents/app/main.py?ref=9ccc096f65dd9fe84ed5affb1fa8a073f6d1d744,https://api.github.com/repositories/999937896/git/blobs/1815a96355f9de8e5a80ee7eba0b8fa119acc0fe,https://github.com/ujsolon/streamlit_chat/blob/9ccc096f65dd9fe84ed5affb1fa8a073f6d1d744/app/main.py,,,0,0,0,19,2025-06-03T11:53:02Z,0,0,"# GenAI PDF Chatbot

A Streamlit-based application that lets you upload PDF documents and chat with them using advanced retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) powered by FAISS vector search and Azure OpenAI (ChatGPT) via LangChain.

---

## Features

- **PDF Upload & Extraction:** Upload one or more PDF files. Text is extracted using `pdfplumber`.
- **Chunking & Embedding:** Documents are chunked and embedded using OpenAI or SentenceTransformers models.
- **Vector Search:** Fast, scalable similarity search using FAISS (default) or a simple in-memory store.
- **Conversational QA:** Ask questions about your documents. The app retrieves relevant chunks and crafts a context-aware prompt for ChatGPT.
- **Streamlit UI:** Clean, interactive interface for uploading, chatting, and managing documents.

---

## Getting Started

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/streamlit_tm.git
cd streamlit_tm
```

### 2. Set Up the Environment

```bash
python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Configure Environment Variables

Copy `.env.sample` to `.env` and fill in your Azure OpenAI and embedding deployment details:

```
OPENAI_API_KEY=xxxx # example ADaEEe1y9SMeua3mZy1i6qcc1auu8x67
OPENAI_API_VERSION=xxxx # example 2024-12-01-preview
OPENAI_CHAT_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=xxxx # example gpt-4o
OPENAI_EMBEDDING_DEPLOYMENT_NAME=xxxx # example text-embedding-ada-002
AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://xxxxxxx.api.cognitive.microsoft.com/ # If using Azure OpenAI, input the endpoint URL here. If using OpenAI, you can remove it.
```

### 4. Run the App

```bash
streamlit run app/main.py
```

---

## Project Structure

```
streamlit_tm/
│
├── app/
│   └── main.py                # Streamlit app entry point
├── src/
│   ├── document_processor/
│   │   └── pdf_extractor.py   # PDF text extraction
│   ├── llm/
│   │   └── chatgpt_client.py  # LangChain ChatGPT client
│   └── vector_store/
│       ├── faiss_store.py     # FAISS vector store
│       └── simple_store.py    # Simple in-memory vector store
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.sample
├── project_journal.md         # Design journal and decisions
└── README.md
```

---

## Usage

1. **Upload PDFs:** Use the sidebar to upload one or more PDF files.
2. **Ask Questions:** Type your question in the chat input. The app retrieves relevant document chunks and queries ChatGPT.

---

## Customization

- **Vector Store:** By default, uses FAISS with OpenAI embeddings. You can switch to `SimpleVectorStore` for prototyping.
- **LLM Model:** Supports OpenAI and Azure OpenAI deployments. Update the `.env` file and sidebar settings as needed.
- **Chunk Size:** Adjust chunking logic in `main.py` for different document types.

---

## Troubleshooting

- Ensure your `.env` is correctly set and API keys are valid.
- If you encounter FAISS or embedding errors, check your Python and package versions.
- For large PDFs, processing may take longer due to embedding and indexing.

---

## References

- [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io/)
