base.py,.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py,5a53203f2e36c8e55559c5925f5f61f1d87bb780,aakashrana7/CorpParse-LangChain_Agent_for_Company_Data_Extraction,https://api.github.com/repositories/1036821892/contents/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py?ref=5150b7e3a32dc503f3d0da9c8d79b0de3ed4d776,https://api.github.com/repositories/1036821892/git/blobs/5a53203f2e36c8e55559c5925f5f61f1d87bb780,https://github.com/aakashrana7/CorpParse-LangChain_Agent_for_Company_Data_Extraction/blob/5150b7e3a32dc503f3d0da9c8d79b0de3ed4d776/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py,LangChain Company Info Extractor (LCEL Agentic Workflow),,0,0,0,6,2025-08-19T21:13:54Z,0,0,"# CorpParse — LCEL-Powered Company Info Extractor

## Project Summary
**CorpParse** is a lightweight pipeline that uses LangChain’s LCEL (Runnable) patterns and an agent-driven workflow to locate and extract structured company details from free-form text. The tool processes text **paragraph-by-paragraph**, identifies company names, founding dates, and founders, and outputs a normalized CSV (`company_info.csv`) for downstream use.

This project is aimed at researchers, analysts, and data engineers who need an automated, repeatable way to convert narrative business descriptions into tabular data.

## File Structure

corpparse/
│
├── backend/
│   ├── app.py                # Flask server (handles frontend routes & API)
│   ├── agent_workflow.py     # LCEL + AI Agent workflow logic (parsing + CSV generation)
│   ├── utils.py              # Helper functions (e.g., PDF text extraction, date handling)
│   └── company_info.csv      # Output CSV file
│
├── frontend/
│   ├── index.html            # UI page (input essay/upload PDF)
│   ├── styles.css            # Styling for frontend
│   └── script.js             # JS to send input to Flask and display results
│
├── requirements.txt          # Dependencies
└── README.md                 # Documentation


## Key Features
- Paragraph-level processing (each paragraph treated as one input unit)
- Agentic extraction pipeline using LangChain LCEL Runnables
- Tool wrappers for deterministic parsing (dates, names) and post-processing
- Output: standardized CSV with one row per discovered company
- Easy to extend (add more fields, integrate vector DBs, or connect to a database)
"
base.py,.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py,5a53203f2e36c8e55559c5925f5f61f1d87bb780,goutam6376/Medical-Appointment-Scheduling-Agent,https://api.github.com/repositories/1049548462/contents/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py?ref=07a019784b3af605c14c5437325cc409669a39ff,https://api.github.com/repositories/1049548462/git/blobs/5a53203f2e36c8e55559c5925f5f61f1d87bb780,https://github.com/goutam6376/Medical-Appointment-Scheduling-Agent/blob/07a019784b3af605c14c5437325cc409669a39ff/.venv/Lib/site-packages/langchain/retrievers/self_query/base.py,,,0,0,0,1,2025-09-03T06:33:12Z,0,0,"# Medical Appointment Scheduling Agent

End-to-end **medical appointment scheduling agent** with Streamlit UI, LangGraph multi-agent orchestration,
Excel calendar simulation, patient lookup against a synthetic EMR (CSV), insurance capture, confirmation export,
form distribution (PDF), and reminder workflow (email/SMS simulated).

> Built for the RagaAI Data Science Intern case study. Uses **Option 1: LangGraph + LangChain**.

## Quick Start

```bash
# 1) Create a venv
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate  # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

# 2) Install deps
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3) Configure (optional) secrets
cp .env.example .env  # then fill in OPENAI_API_KEY, SMTP/Twilio if you have them

# 4) Run the app
streamlit run app.py
```

The app auto-generates:
- `data/patients.csv` — 50 synthetic patients
- `data/doctors_schedule.xlsx` — three doctors' available slots for the next 7 days
- `data/appointments.xlsx` — confirmed bookings log (on demand)

## Features
- Patient greeting & validation
- Patient lookup (new vs returning) using fuzzy match on Name + DOB
- Smart scheduling (60 min new, 30 min returning)
- Calendar availability visualization and booking (Excel-backed)
- Insurance capture
- Confirmation export to Excel + simulated email
- Intake form distribution (PDF attachment from `templates/`)
- 3-step reminder workflow (simulated email/SMS with interactive status toggle)

## Tech Stack
- **LangGraph + LangChain** for agent workflow
- **Streamlit** for UI
- **Pandas / OpenPyXL** for CSV/Excel
- **FuzzyWuzzy** for patient lookup
- **.env** for secrets (optional)

## Notes
- If no `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set, the app falls back to light rule-based prompts.
- Email/SMS are simulated to logs; real providers (SMTP/Twilio) used only if credentials are present.

## Demo Flow
1. Start chat → collect name, DOB, preferred doctor/location.
2. Lookup in EMR → new vs returning.
3. Show calendar slots → select an available slot.
4. Capture insurance → confirm appointment.
5. Export to Excel → send confirmation + intake form PDF.
6. Schedule reminders → track confirmations/cancellation reason.

---

### Files
- `app.py` — Streamlit UI + LangGraph runner
- `langgraph_workflow.py` — Defines agents and the graph
- `agents/` — Specialized agent functions
- `utils/` — Data gen, calendar, comms, export, config
- `templates/New Patient Intake Form.pdf` — Email after confirmation (provided)

**Good luck!**
"
